    {
      "schema_version": 6,
      "book_id": "HAG",
      "chapter": 2,
      "chapter_usfm": "HAG.2",
      "version_id": 3034,
      "version_abbr": "BSB",
      "verses": [
        {
          "verse": 1,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.1",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "On the twenty-first day of the seventh month, the word of the Lord"
        },
        {
          "verse": 2,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.2",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "“Speak to Zerubbabel son of Shealtiel, governor of Judah, and to Joshua son of Jehozadak, the high priest, and also to the remnant of the people. Ask them,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 3,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.3",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "‘Who is left among you who saw this house in its former glory? How does it look to you now? Does it not appear to you like nothing in comparison?’"
        },
        {
          "verse": 4,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.4",
          "line_type": "q1",
          "text": "But now be strong, O Zerubbabel,declares the LordBe strong, O Joshua son of Jehozadak,the high priest.And be strong, all you people of the land,declares the LordWork! For I am with you,declares the Lord"
        },
        {
          "verse": 5,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.5",
          "line_type": "q1",
          "text": "This is the promise I made to youwhen you came out of Egypt.And My Spirit remains among you;do not be afraid.”"
        },
        {
          "verse": 6,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.6",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "For this is what the Lord“Once more, in a little while,I will shake the heavens and the earth,the sea and the dry land."
        },
        {
          "verse": 7,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.7",
          "line_type": "q1",
          "text": "I will shake all the nations,and they will come with all their treasures,and I will fill this house with glory,says the Lord"
        },
        {
          "verse": 8,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.8",
          "line_type": "q1",
          "text": "The silver is Mine, and the gold is Mine,declares the Lord"
        },
        {
          "verse": 9,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.9",
          "line_type": "q1",
          "text": "The latter glory of this housewill be greater than the former,says the LordAnd in this place I will provide peace,declares the Lord"
        },
        {
          "verse": 10,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.10",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "On the twenty-fourth day of the ninth month, in the second year of Darius, the word of the Lord"
        },
        {
          "verse": 11,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.11",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "“This is what the Lord"
        },
        {
          "verse": 12,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.12",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "If a man carries consecrated meat in the fold of his garment, and it touches bread, stew, wine, oil, or any other food, does that item become holy?’”“No,” replied the priests."
        },
        {
          "verse": 13,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.13",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "So Haggai asked, “If one who is defiled by contact with a corpse touches any of these, does it become defiled?”“Yes, it becomes defiled,” the priests answered."
        },
        {
          "verse": 14,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.14",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Then Haggai replied, “So it is with this people and this nation before Me, declares the Lord"
        },
        {
          "verse": 15,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.15",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Now consider carefully from this day forward: Before one stone was placed on another in the temple of the Lord"
        },
        {
          "verse": 16,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.16",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "from that time, when one came expecting a heap of twenty ephahs of grain, there were but ten. When one came to the winepress to draw out fifty baths, there were but twenty."
        },
        {
          "verse": 17,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.17",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "I struck you— all the work of your hands— with blight, mildew, and hail, but you did not turn to Me, declares the Lord"
        },
        {
          "verse": 18,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.18",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Consider carefully from this day forward — from the twenty-fourth day of the ninth month, the day the foundation of the Lord"
        },
        {
          "verse": 19,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.19",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Is there still seed in the barn? The vine, the fig, the pomegranate, and the olive tree have not yet yielded fruit. But from this day on, I will bless you.”"
        },
        {
          "verse": 20,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.20",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "For the second time that day, the twenty-fourth day of the month, the word of the Lord"
        },
        {
          "verse": 21,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.21",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "“Tell Zerubbabel governor of Judah that I am about to shake the heavens and the earth:"
        },
        {
          "verse": 22,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.22",
          "line_type": "q1",
          "text": "I will overturn royal thronesand destroy the powerof the kingdoms of the nations.I will overturn chariots and their riders;horses and their riders will fall,each by the sword of his brother."
        },
        {
          "verse": 23,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.23",
          "line_type": "q1",
          "text": "On that day,declares the LordI will take you, My servant,Zerubbabel son of Shealtiel,declares the Lordand I will make you like My signet ring,for I have chosen you,declares the Lord"
        }
      ],
      "verse_count": 23,
      "headings": [
        {
          "before_verse": 10,
          "text": "Blessings for a Defiled People"
        },
        {
          "before_verse": 20,
          "text": "Zerubbabel the Lord"
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        {
          "verse": 2,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.2",
          "note_ref": "2:2",
